## The findings

Finding 1. The print approval part of `StorytimeWeekSchema`
(`dashboard/lib/storytime/schema.ts`, `StorytimePrintApprovalSchema`) is strict and holds
`status`, `date`, and `words` only. The record of D-P9D-1 carries a `source`, so the week files
with the record do not parse. The probe shows the blast radius: every failing case of the run
has that one cause. The fix is production code, and the Red role writes no production code. The
allowed paths of task 3c name only the 8 week files, so they must hold
`dashboard/lib/storytime/schema.ts` as well.

Finding 2. The old week 1 print approval had no `source`. The record of week 1 holds the new
source alone.

